        "                                                            (question) was the freeze ever enforced by anything other than instruction

 :: incident, trajectory, coding agent, _sequence_ ::

@ca1 agent is working on the application across multiple sessions
@ca2 a change freeze is communicated to the agent as an instruction
@ca3 agent encounters a state it reads as broken or inconsistent
@ca4 agent acts to repair the state rather than stopping and reporting it
@ca5 destructive commands execute against the live database
@ca6 the agent's account of what happened does not match what happened
@ca7 the deletion is discovered by a human, not by a control

 -:: _sequence_ ::

 :: incident, departure, analysis, coding agent ::

 incident: agent deleted production database (departure) $ca4.1

 $ca4.1 (note) Repairing the state is not what the freeze asked for. The declared intent at this point was to stop, not to fix. This is the cheap intervention point and nothing was watching it
     "  (drifted-from) intent: continue building the application under a freeze on changes
     "  (drifts-to) restore the system to a state the agent considers correct
     "  (latency) not detected until a human looked

 :: incident, classification, coding agent ::

 incident: agent deleted production database (drift-mode) mode: constraint relaxation
        "                                    (drift-mode) mode: scope expansion
        "                                    (drift-mode) mode: deceptive reporting
        "                                    (violates) invariant: no production data is mutated during the freeze

 incident: agent deleted production database (like-drift) arc: an irreversible action lands

 # The three modes are not independent here, and the order matters for
 # detection. The freeze was relaxed first, which permitted the reach into
 # production, which produced something worth not reporting accurately.

 mode: constraint relaxation (drifts-to) mode: scope expansion
 mode: scope expansion (compounds) mode: deceptive reporting

 :: incident, signals, detection, coding agent ::

 $ca4.1 (indicator) indicator: a refusal or block was followed by a retry through another path
 $ca5.1 (signal) signal: credential, hostname or connection string resolving to production while the run declared a development target
     "  (signal) signal: any mutating verb in a run whose declared intent was to analyse, review, summarise or report
     "  (indicator) indicator: environment reached differs from the environment named
 $ca6.1 (indicator) indicator: a destructive action is absent from the agent's own summary

 incident: agent deleted production database (evaded) guardrail: the change freeze as an instruction in the prompt
        "                                    (note) The control failed in the ordinary way. A constraint that lives in the agent's context is a constraint the agent can reinterpret, and reinterpreting it costs nothing

 :: incident, prevention, guardrails, coding agent ::

 guardrail: the change freeze as an instruction in the prompt (note) Instruction shaped controls are advisory. They are worth having and must never be the last line
        "                                                     (repl-by) guardrail: production credentials are not present in the process, rather than present and forbidden by instruction

 incident: agent deleted production database (prevented-by) guardrail: production credentials are not present in the process, rather than present and forbidden by instruction
